# Origin:  clearcotelabs/clearcote-browser -- the fabrication shape, not the code.
# Source:  patches/180-geolocation.patch
# Commit:  clearcote-browser-main tarball, audited 2026-08-24 (Veil/docs/MIGRATION-UNGOOGLED.md 6.5)
# License: BSD-3-Clause (see CREDITS.md), same terms as the code it edits.
# Changes: re-authored. What transferred from `180` is the *shape* -- answer `QueryNextPosition()`
#          with a fabricated `Geoposition` built from a "--fingerprint-location=lat,lng" read,
#          `accuracy = 100`, Chromium's own no-sensor sentinels for altitude/heading/speed, and a
#          task-runner-posted `PositionChanged()`. What does not:
#          `180` re-parses the switch on every request, and its version answers before the
#          permission machinery has had its say; the parse here is once per process, and the
#          fabricated answer is delivered only from `QueryNextPosition()`, which the permission
#          flow reaches only after `OnGeolocationPermissionStatusUpdated` reports GRANTED -- a
#          denial goes to `HandlePermissionError()` and never here -- so a persona cannot make a
#          page that was never granted read coordinates (measured,
#          Veil/docs/MIGRATION-UNGOOGLED.md 6.22).
#
#          `is_precise` is left at its mojom default and `altitude` is the `kBadAltitude` sentinel
#          rather than 0 -- `CreateGeoposition()` maps anything <= -10000 m to `nullopt`, which is
#          what a desktop without a barometer reports.
#
# Veil-authored `9NN` numbering: `970` has no `070` to correct; `950`-`999` are Veil-authored with
# no counterpart.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The last of `000`'s four declared-but-unread switches.
#
# `000` has declared `--fingerprint-location` and propagated it to every renderer since it was
# ported, and no patch in the set read it -- the mirror image of the Stage 1 lie, living in the
# tree rather than on Veil's command line. T22 reads it, and Veil's `to_engine_args` gains the
# arm in the same task, in the order 6.9 fixed: the patch lands, the read is measured, *then* the
# switch leaves NOT_IN_TIER_ONE (Veil/docs/STAGE-6-FULL-COVERAGE.md 1).
#
# Why a switch at all, when the persona already carries a seed: the coordinates are the one surface
# the user has to be able to point at. Veil is offline and holds no geo-IP table, so the engine
# cannot derive a plausible position from the proxy exit the way T19's `--webrtc-ip` does for the
# srflx candidate; a seed-derived coordinate would put the persona in a field or an ocean beside a
# timezone it cannot agree with. The value is therefore declared, and `veil_core::validate` owns
# the proxy-exit <-> timezone <-> coordinate agreement (6.22) -- the engine cannot check it, so the
# configuration layer must. The switch is deliberately not consulted with `--disable-spoofing`:
# it is not a spoof of a host surface -- the host has no coordinates to restore -- and the opt-out
# is deleting the value from the profile.
#
# Nothing moves without the switch: with no `--fingerprint-location` the fabricated position is
# `nullopt` and `QueryNextPosition()` is byte-for-byte the stock call.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/geolocation/geolocation.cc
